# Ebb — Seats

## Contract

The seat contract — what a seat is, seat accounting, the rules, launching, and the standing prompt — is `contracts/SEATS.md` in the template repo, copied verbatim into `wheelhouse/fleet/SEATS.md` at install. It is not reproduced here, and it is not edited per-project.

This specimen shows only what the interview writes: the roster below.

## This project

### Roster

| Seat | Role brief | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `seat-worker-1` | `wheelhouse/fleet/WORKER.md` | Primary implementation |
| `seat-reviewer` | `wheelhouse/crew/REVIEWER.md` | Never authors what it reviews |
| (commander) | this folder's `CLAUDE.md` | The principal's own session |

Minimum viable fleet for this project. A second worker goes in when the reviewer is idle waiting for work; a designer goes in when the principal is spending more time decomposing beads than deciding direction.

---

## What the installed file actually looks like

This specimen shows only the generated half. The file at `wheelhouse/fleet/SEATS.md` in a real project is:

```
# Fleet: Seats
<intro line>

## Contract                 <- copied verbatim from contracts/SEATS.md, never edited
  ### What a seat is
  ### Seat accounting       <- one seat = one subscription = one human beneficiary
  ### Rules
  ### Launching a seat
  ### Standing prompt
  ### Minimum viable fleet

## This project             <- everything from here down is generated, and is the
  ### Roster                   only part this specimen shows
```

If your installed file is missing the contract half, the install split it in the wrong place. That has happened; see the note in `BOOTSTRAP.md` about matching the heading exactly.
